While showing off his arcade games, host Joe La Puma asked which game Ross is unbeatable in, and that&#8217;s when Rozay revealed he has a near-decadelong winning streak when it comes to the popular football game. &#8220;I haven&#8217;t lost in Madden in maybe eight or nine years,&#8221; he claimed. &#8220;I used to smoke, sip syrup, and now I could sit there and I could sit there while listening to a beat at the same time.&#8221;

He was then asked if he has a specific team that he plays with, to which Ross replied that he has three teams he goes to depending on who his opponent picks. &#8220;I can&#8217;t disclose who I play with,&#8221; he said. &#8220;If you ever want any smoke or if somebody wants some smoke, depending on who you are and where you from, then I&#8217;ll decide. I got three teams that I could go with. It just depends what I want to exploit you on the most.&#8221;

However, when it comes to celebrities, Ross said that he tries to avoid playing his famous friends because their ego could sometimes get the best of them. &#8220;Not really,&#8221; he replied after being asked if a celebrity has ever challenged him in Madden . &#8220;You know celebrities have egos and they know I&#8217;ll text them early in the morning, &#8216;I toasted you. Are you embarrassed?&#8217; That sh&#8211; go a long way.

